@baseUrl = http://localhost:5248
@adminApiKey = replace-with-CUDAPYTHON_ADMIN_KEY

### API readiness
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/info

### Bundled Python environment metadata
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/info/python-environment

### Validate Python packages and CUDA binding imports
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/info/python-environment/validation

### CUDA driver version and initialization status
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/info/cuda/driver

### CUDA device specifications
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/info/cuda/devices

### Discover a page of CUDA Python functions
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cuda-python/functions?modulePrefix=cuda.bindings.driver&offset=0&limit=100

### Search discovered CUDA Python functions
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cuda-python/functions?search=driver&offset=0&limit=25

### Invoke a public CUDA Python callable (requires a usable NVIDIA driver)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/cuda-python/invoke
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{adminApiKey}}

{
  "moduleName": "cuda.bindings.driver",
  "attributePath": "cuDriverGetVersion",
  "arguments": [],
  "keywordArguments": {}
}

### Stage the latest compatible Python environment (Development only; activation requires restart)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/maintenance/python-environment/update
X-API-Key: {{adminApiKey}}

### Build the win-x64 NuGet package (Development only; requires a local repository and .NET SDK)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/maintenance/nuget/build
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{adminApiKey}}

{
  "configuration": "Release"
}
